messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2024,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2025,
      "event": "AI automation displaces millions of knowledge workers.",
      "detail": "Large language models and robotics integrated into workflows cause structural unemployment, prompting universal basic income trials in several nations."
    },
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "Engineered pandemic or lab accident causes global health crisis.",
      "detail": "A modified pathogen escapes containment, killing millions and leading to permanent global biodefense infrastructure and travel restrictions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Arctic becomes ice-free in summer; Atlantic Meridional Overturning Circulation weakens.",
      "detail": "Climate tipping points trigger accelerated warming, causing crop failures and mass migration from tropical regions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "First clinically approved germline gene editing in humans.",
      "detail": "CRISPR-based therapies eliminate hereditary diseases like Huntington's, sparking debate over genetic enhancement and leading to an international treaty banning heritable cognitive modifications."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Commercial nuclear fusion achieves net energy gain.",
      "detail": "Private and public reactors begin replacing fossil fuels, driving energy costs down and enabling large-scale desalination and carbon capture."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "Artificial general intelligence (AGI) is achieved.",
      "detail": "AI systems surpass human performance in most cognitive tasks, leading to rapid scientific progress but also existential risk concerns and economic restructuring."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "First permanent Mars settlement established.",
      "detail": "A city of 1,000 people achieves food self-sufficiency using local resources, marking humanity's transition to a multi-planetary species."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Global human population peaks at approximately 10.4 billion.",
      "detail": "Fertility rates drop below replacement in most regions due to urbanization and education, beginning a long-term decline that eases resource pressures."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Longevity escape velocity reached in developed nations.",
      "detail": "Senolytics, gene therapy, and organ regeneration extend healthy lifespan beyond 120 years, fundamentally altering retirement, economics, and family structures."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Brain-computer interfaces become mainstream.",
      "detail": "Non-invasive and implantable devices allow direct neural control of computers, memory augmentation, and thought-to-text communication, blurring the line between human and machine cognition."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Solar radiation management deployed to stabilize global temperatures.",
      "detail": "Stratospheric aerosol injection limits warming to 2.5 degrees Celsius but creates geopolitical tensions over regional weather patterns and terminates only gradually."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "First large-scale space habitats constructed in Earth orbit.",
      "detail": "O'Neill cylinders housing 100,000 people each begin manufacturing using asteroid materials, creating a space-based economy independent of Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Global carbon emissions reach net zero.",
      "detail": "Direct air capture and renewable energy stabilize atmospheric CO2 at 450 ppm, though sea levels continue rising for centuries due to thermal inertia."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Breakthrough Starshot probes launched toward Alpha Centauri.",
      "detail": "Laser-propelled gram-scale spacecraft travel at 20% light speed, reaching the system in 20 years and transmitting data back by 2160."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Asteroid mining makes rare metals abundant on Earth.",
      "detail": "Platinum-group metals and water from near-Earth asteroids flood markets, enabling advanced manufacturing and making space launch economically trivial."
    },
    {
      "year": 2180,
      "event": "First successful whole-brain emulation of a human mind.",
      "detail": "A human consciousness is uploaded to a digital substrate, proving mind uploading possible though raising philosophical questions about personal identity and continuity."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Post-human era begins as digital and enhanced beings dominate.",
      "detail": "The majority of intelligent entities on Earth are now digital minds or genetically enhanced humans, with baseline biological humans becoming a protected minority."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Self-replicating von Neumann probes begin industrializing the asteroid belt.",
      "detail": "Autonomous machines mine and replicate using local materials, exponentially increasing the solar system's industrial capacity without human labor."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Solar system population exceeds one billion, mostly in habitats.",
      "detail": "Millions live in rotating space habitats and terraformed Mars, with Earth's population declining as people migrate to orbital cities with controlled environments."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Genetic speciation occurs between enhanced and baseline humans.",
      "detail": "Cumulative genetic modifications create reproductive isolation, leading to distinct post-human species with vastly different cognitive and physical capabilities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "First extrasolar colony established at Tau Ceti.",
      "detail": "A generation ship launched in 2300 arrives with 10,000 colonists, establishing a self-sufficient civilization on an exoplanet 12 light-years away."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "Dyson swarm captures ten percent of solar output.",
      "detail": "Billions of energy-collecting satellites surround the Sun, providing near-limitless power and enabling the construction of megastructures throughout the inner solar system."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Civilization achieves Kardashev Type II status.",
      "detail": "Humanity harnesses the total energy output of the Sun, allowing control of planetary climates and the beginning of stellar engineering projects."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Hundreds of interstellar colonies exist within 100 light-years.",
      "detail": "Relativistic ships and sleeper vessels have spread human-descended civilizations across nearby star systems, connected by laser communication networks."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "First contact with an alien technological civilization.",
      "detail": "SETI detects and establishes communication with an ancient civilization in the galactic core, or alternatively, confirms the Great Filter hypothesis by finding no other signals."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Expansion to neighboring galaxies begins.",
      "detail": "Relativistic ark ships traveling at near-light speed depart for the Magellanic Clouds, carrying uploaded minds in robust substrates to seed new civilizations."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Biological Homo sapiens is extinct.",
      "detail": "The last unmodified humans die out, leaving only post-human descendants—digital, cybernetic, or genetically engineered—who carry human heritage."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Stellar engineering projects reshape the local stellar neighborhood.",
      "detail": "Stars are moved using Shkadov thrusters or star lifting to create optimal configurations for long-term habitability and energy harvesting."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Energy harvesting from supermassive black holes achieved.",
      "detail": "Civilization extracts rotational energy from black holes via Penrose processes or accretion disk tapping, powering computations at scales previously impossible."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Planning for the ultimate fate of the universe begins.",
      "detail": "Facing the accelerating expansion of the universe, humanity explores options such as migrating to younger galaxies, creating baby universes, or transitioning to a purely informational existence."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity exists as a multi-galactic post-biological civilization.",
      "detail": "Descendants of humanity—now purely informational or exotic matter-based—span thousands of galaxies, having transcended biological form and individual mortality."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "There is a significant probability (roughly 30-50%) that humanity or its descendants suffer an existential catastrophe—such as unaligned AGI, engineered pandemics, or nuclear war—before the year 3000; however, assuming survival, the most likely trajectory is a transition to a post-human, multi-planetary civilization that eventually spreads across the galaxy, with biological Homo sapiens becoming extinct or transformed long before 10000."
}
